# Project.md sync (Nove Work)

`Project.md` is the source of truth for chapter AI strategy: chapter-card outlines, pre-generate, refine, word-count rules, and chapter memory.

When you change any of the following, **update `Project.md` in the same change**:

- `generate_chapter` / `preview_generate_chapter` / `refine_chapter` / `save_chapter` / `preview_chapter_outline_brief` / `generate_chapter_cards` / `plan_next_chapters` / `generate_chapter_plots` / `regenerate_chapter_memory` / `set_chapter_memory`
- Related prompts in `src-tauri/src/prompts.rs` (`generate_chapter_*`, `refine_chapter_*`, `repair_*`, `outline_gen_brief`, `gen_chapter_cards_*`, `plan_next_chapters_*`, `gen_chapter_plots_*`, `extract_chapter_memory_*`)
- `chapter_constraints.rs`, chapter memory extract/store timing, or `WORD_COUNT_TOLERANCE`
- Workspace UI behavior for those flows (root generate cards, refine modes, memory panels)

## How to update

1. Edit the matching section (§0 concepts, §1 outlines, §2 generate, §3 refine, §4 length, §5 memory, §6 UI).
2. Adjust the checklists if steps or entry points change.
3. Do not leave `Project.md` describing removed passes (e.g. length-repair LLM, memory-on-generate).

UI copy still follows `i18n-sync.mdc`; this rule is for strategy/docs only.
